<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  WinUI's own button styles (generic.xaml, Windows App SDK 1.8), copied verbatim except for ONE
  thing: the 83 ms BrushTransition on the Background is removed.

  Why: that fade interpolates straight between two brushes' ARGB values. Whenever they differ in
  alpha - the near-clear resting fill vs a hover colour, a transparent segmented button vs its
  selected fill, or EVERY button at once when Light/Dark is switched - the midpoint is a
  half-transparent grey, which shows as a bright flash. No property or lightweight-styling key
  turns it off; the template is the only place it lives. Without it the change is instant, as it
  was in the MAUI app.

  Re-copy these (scratchpad nofade.py did it) if the Windows App SDK is upgraded.
-->
